<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/9th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Lalakaon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">863</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Poson · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arab-byzantine-wars">Arab–Byzantine wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Lalakaon was fought on 3 September 863 in Paphlagonia, in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a>, between a Byzantine army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petronas">Petronas</a> and the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umar-al-aqta">Umar al-Aqta</a>, emir of Melitene, who had sacked Amisos on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> encircled the Arab army and destroyed it, killing Umar. The victory marked the start of Byzantium's offensive on its eastern frontier.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-lalakaon.jpg" alt="Battle of Lalakaon" width="320" height="163" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown, 13th-century author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fighting_between_Byzantines_and_Arabs_Chronikon_of_Ioannis_Skylitzes,_end_of_13th_century..jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
